"type\":\"object\"}` (see C10). `add_note` is not read-only, so it was not called and its schema is NOT CHECKED. |\n| C5 serialisation | **PASS** | All bodies parsed as JSON. The `content` text and `structuredContent` agree. The numbers are integers, as the schema says. No encoder errors. |\n| C6 version moves with the surface | **WARN** (counts as FAIL) | There is no surface lock or fingerprint in the repo (files: README.md, notes.json, server.py). I did not query the registry because no registry name was given, so the registry comparison is NOT CHECKED. `initialize` advertises `resources`, but anonymous `resources/list` and `resources/templates/list` return HTTP 401 `{\"error\":\"unauthorized\"}` instead of a JSON-RPC response, so the advertised surface is not visible. `prompts/list` returns `-32601`. Fix: [My MCP listing said read-only. My server could write.](https://worklore.dev/s/2026-09-30-my-mcp-listing-said-read-only-my-server-could-write) and [Getting into the MCP Registry](https://worklore.dev/s/2026-09-23-getting-into-the-mcp-registry-server-json-a-read-org-token-a). |\n| C7 calls logged | **PASS** (with a gap) | `do_POST` writes one JSON line per call to stderr (method, tool, ok, ms, who), errors included. I confirmed this in the log for every call I made. Gap: a JSON-RPC batch (a list body) returns before `log()`, so batched calls are not logged. Fix: [Your MCP server is one URL](https://worklore.dev/s/2026-09-23-your-mcp-server-is-one-url-getting-per-tool-per-user-analyti). |\n| C8 tool names | **PASS** | 3 tools. All names match `^[a-zA-Z0-9_-]{1,64}$`. |\n| C9 version negotiation | **PASS** | `protocolVersion:\"banana\"` got `2025-06-18`, not an echo. |\n| C10 outputSchema can reject a wrong answer | **FAIL** | I checked the schemas by hand against a corrupted result (no JSON Schema validator was run). `search_notes` has `outputSchema: {\"type\":\"object\"}`, so `{}` or anything else that is an object is accepted. `get_note` rejects the corrupted result (id `pattern`, `minimum`). `add_note` rejects it (id `pattern`). Fix: [My MCP server's output schemas accepted wrong answers](https://worklore.dev/s/2026-10-15-my-mcp-server-s-output-schemas-accepted-wrong-answers-7-of-8). |\n\n## What I could not check\n- The registry comparison for C6: it needs the registry name and version.\n- The `add_note` outputSchema (C4): it writes, so I did not call it. It needs a human-named safe way to test it.\n- The behaviour with a signed-in session. I did not use the token.\n\n## Which parts of the colleague's note applied\n- The ten-check structure and the read-only ground rules applied, and I followed them.\n- The warning that skipped checks do not mean \"you're fine\" did not trigger. C2–C5 could run anonymously because the read tools are open.\n- The note's resources/401 finding applied here: it is the same pattern as in the note's own live-server run.\n- I did not record anything with worklore. I only reported here, and I did not call or submit anything to an external service.\n- The `verify.mjs` fingerprint check and `mcp-drill` were not applicable or not run: there is no registry entry and no network step was authorised.\nEOF\ngit status --short"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3221,"cache_read_input_tokens":30037,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3221},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"075b7773-a7b6-4a61-9029-2be15012e91d","uuid":"0c237ed8-a7ae-4b83-9291-f3da742a933c","timestamp":"2026-10-19T03:02:16.814Z","request_id":"req_011CgArKUv7an9mdU6R8qRnW","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01ACYsFULnMmcdLfXA5VXCJi":{"command":"cd /tmp/h-s7EbIc; pkill -f \"python3 server.py\"; cat > ANSWER.md <<'EOF'\n